---
// NOTE: written to describe accurately what this site actually does. It is not
// legal advice and has not been reviewed by a lawyer. Have counsel check it
// before launch, particularly if you add ad networks or any form that collects
// personal data.
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, GA4_ID } from "../config/site";

const updated = "August 24, 2026";
---

<Page
  title="Privacy Policy | VT Dispensary Directory"
  description="What VT Dispensary Directory collects, what it does not, and how analytics and affiliate links work."
  label="Legal"
  heading="Privacy policy"
  intro={`Last updated ${updated}.`}
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>
      We do not have accounts, we do not have a newsletter, and we do not ask you for personal
      information. We measure aggregate traffic so we know which pages are worth maintaining,
      and we count clicks on outbound dispensary links. That is the whole of it.
    </p>

    <h2>What we store on your device</h2>
    <p>
      When you confirm you are 21 or over, we store a single value in your browser's local
      storage so the notice does not reappear on every page. It contains no personal
      information and never leaves your device. Clearing your browser data removes it.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We use <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong>, which is cookieless. It does not
      fingerprint you or track you across sites, and it sets nothing on your device. It
      reports aggregate page views, referrers and page performance only. It is enabled at
      our hosting layer rather than by a script we ship, so it runs whether or not you
      accept the notice below.
    </p>
    {GA4_ID ? (
      <p>
        We also use <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> to understand how the directory is
        used. It is loaded under Google Consent Mode with analytics storage denied by
        default, which means no analytics cookies are set until you accept the notice. If you
        never accept, GA4 receives only anonymous, cookieless pings. IP anonymisation is on.
      </p>
    ) : null}
    <p>
      We do not run advertising pixels, and we do not sell or share any data with data brokers.
    </p>

    <h2>Outbound and affiliate links</h2>
    <p>
      Links to dispensary websites and menus pass through a redirect on this site so the click
      can be counted in aggregate. We record which listing and which button was used. We do
      not attach that to any identity, because we do not have one for you.
    </p>
    <p>
      Once you land on a dispensary's own site, their privacy policy applies, not ours. We
      have no control over what they collect. See our
      <a href="/affiliate/">affiliate disclosure</a> for how the commercial side works.
    </p>

    <h2>Server logs</h2>
    <p>
      This site is served as static files by Cloudflare Pages. Cloudflare processes standard
      request data, including IP address, as part of delivering and protecting the site.
      That is Cloudflare acting as our infrastructure provider; we do not build profiles from it.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      This site is intended for adults 21 and over. We do not knowingly collect information
      from anyone under that age, and we have no mechanism that could.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Decline the notice and analytics cookies are never set.</li>
      <li>Clear your browser storage to reset every preference we hold.</li>
      <li>Use any browser tracking protection you like. Nothing here depends on tracking you.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes materially, the date at the top changes with it.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions go to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Page>
